.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/results-rework-02.md:58:Initial reservation owns window plus fixed read/write/metadata capacity. Four successive fully-consumed replenishment cycles restore outstanding credit to the immutable cap with `newlyReservedBytes == 0` after the first capacity expansion; lane, global-window, and ledger totals remain byte-identical.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/results-rework-02.md-59-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/results-rework-02.md-60-`openFailure`, `normalClose`, `reset`, `cancellation`, `laneFailure`, and `lateCallback` share one idempotent release transition. The first owned release returns exact window and ledger bytes; an absent or duplicate release returns zero without retaining the channel UUID. A deterministic `10_000`-channel test performs unknown callbacks followed by open/release for the same IDs and finishes with zero active reservations and exact metrics, proving that idempotency has no unbounded release-tombstone collection. Rekey preserves reservations; `releaseLane` releases every owned row exactly once.
