.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/results-before-rework.md-2-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/results-before-rework.md-3-## Implemented policy
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/results-before-rework.md-4-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/results-before-rework.md-5-Units: KiB = 1024 bytes; bandwidth = integer bits/s; RTT = integer ns. Inputs are capped before multiplication. bulkBytes = clamp(ceil(cappedBandwidth * cappedRTT / 8000000000), bulkMin, bulkMax), using full-width division and saturating sums. relayBytes = min(relayMax, saturatingAdd(relayControl, saturatingMultiply(datagramCount, max(4 + frameBody, 64)))). Initial admission atomically requires channel <= per-channel ceiling, laneReserved + channel <= lane ceiling, globalReserved + channel <= global window ceiling, and committed + window + read + write + metadata <= global ledger ceiling. Adjustment delta = min(cap - outstandingCredit, cap - alreadyReservedWindow, laneHeadroom, globalWindowHeadroom, ledgerHeadroom).
--
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/results-before-rework.md-15-Initial reservation owns window plus fixed read/write/metadata capacity. Adjustment grows the reservation but never beyond the immutable channel cap. openFailure, normalClose, reset, cancellation, laneFailure, and lateCallback all use one idempotent release transition. First release returns exact window and ledger bytes; duplicates return zero. Rekey preserves reservations; releaseLane after failure releases every row exactly once. Metrics expose reservations, adjustment bytes, releases, duplicate releases, released bytes, and typed refusal counts.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/results-before-rework.md-16-
