.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-4-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-5-## Findings
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-6-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md:7:### P1 — Repeated `WINDOW_ADJUST` credit stalls after the reservation reaches its cap
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-8-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-9-Production call site: `SSHReceiveWindowBudgetLedger.reserveAdjustment` in `Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHReceiveWindowBudgetPolicy.swift:517`.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-10-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md:11:The implementation includes `capBytes - reservedWindowBytes` directly in `delta` and increments `reservedWindowBytes` by the full advertised adjustment. This conflates reusable advertised credit with newly reserved capacity. With a 32 KiB initial reservation and a 64 KiB immutable cap, the first low-water adjustment reserves the remaining 32 KiB but advertises only 32 KiB. Once that reserved capacity reaches 64 KiB, every later replenishment is rejected as `noCreditNeeded`, even after the peer has consumed all outstanding credit. A long-lived channel therefore stalls after approximately one cap's worth of data.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-12-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md:13:The binding contract computes adjustment from `channelCap - outstandingAdvertisedCredit` and available ledger headroom; already-reserved but currently unadvertised capacity remains reusable. The decision already has separate `adjustmentBytes` and `newlyReservedBytes` fields, so these values must be calculated separately. The required regression must consume/replenish the same channel for multiple cycles, require credit to return to the immutable cap, require `newlyReservedBytes == 0` once the cap is fully reserved, and keep lane/global/ledger totals unchanged on those later replenishments.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-14-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-15-The existing test at `Tests/ReluxTunnelCoreTests/SSHReceiveWindowBudgetPolicyTests.swift:137` asserts the incorrect refusal and therefore cannot detect this failure.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-16-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md:17:Independent scratch reproduction: `.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/reviewer-replenishment-repro-02.log`, exit 1, terminating with `second_adjustment_refused=noCreditNeeded`. The first harness attempt failed before execution because of a local SwiftPM package-identity mismatch; that setup-only failure is recorded separately as `reviewer-replenishment-repro-01.log` and is not product evidence.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-18-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-19-### P2 — Release tombstones are unbounded
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-20-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/review-verdict.md-21-Production call site: `SSHReceiveWindowBudgetLedger.release` in `Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHReceiveWindowBudgetPolicy.swift:551`.
--
