.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-19-- IMPLEMENTATION: Core selects control, ordinary, capped-BDP bulk, and relay control-plus-UDP-burst initial windows with checked configuration and saturating arithmetic. Initial and earned adjustment credit reserve per-channel, per-lane, global-window, and global-ledger capacity before admission; releases are exact and idempotent.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-20-- GATES: Soft caps only new initial windows. Pressure withholds every adjustment and nonessential opens; Critical, rekeying, failed, closing, closed, stale-generation, low-water, and insufficient-reservation paths refuse without changing or queueing credit. Previously advertised credit is never represented as revoked.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-21-- ADAPTER: Both libssh2 `libssh2_channel_open_ex` call sites use one tested initial-window conversion. The adapter still truthfully reports consumer-driven adjustment as unsupported; no protocol message is sent outside that adapter.
