.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-1145-- COVERAGE: `PacketFlowBridge.swift` plus `PacketFlowBridgeContracts.swift` measure 94.55% line coverage and 88.28% region coverage. Strict Swift format, `swift build`, and the Core boundary guard pass; production sources were not changed.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-1146-- ANOMALY: ThreadSanitizer scheduling exposed a test-observation race where the fake PacketFlow recorded a reverse write before the bridge's subsequent metric increment. The test now waits on the metric boundary explicitly; no product data race or contract defect was found.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-1147-
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-1148-### 1208 — libssh2 adapter hits third-round channel/exec/window API boundary (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md:1149:- BLOCKER: Pinned `ssh2_channel_read` automatically sends WINDOW_ADJUST before returning consumer bytes when remaining credit crosses its private threshold. There is no public manual-window mode, so consumer-earned credit and the immutable advertised cap cannot be enforced.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-1150-- BLOCKER: `ssh2_channel_open` parses all RFC 4254 rejection reasons, then collapses them to `LIBSSH2_ERROR_CHANNEL_FAILURE`; no public typed/numeric reason survives. The remaining diagnostic string is not a stable control-flow API.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-1151-- BLOCKER: Channels store only integer `exit_status` defaulting to zero and an optional signal name. The public API cannot distinguish explicit status 0 from no exit metadata and discards the RFC `core dumped` signal bit.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-1152-- ROUTING: This is the third fork-gap round anticipated by TASK-260720-2sltje. Do not add a partial/mock-only adapter. Recommend failing libssh2 red at M0 unless its value justifies one explicitly approved consolidated fork extension for manual windows, typed open failures, and lossless exec-exit metadata; the alternative is an explicit M0-to-M3/common-contract revision. Exact evidence and resume decision are attached as `TASK-260715-1ozsb6_third-public-api-blocker.md`.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/negative-worktree/LOGBOOK.md-1153-
