.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw-review/warning-floor-mutant/LOGBOOK.md-14-- REWORK: Self-review rejected a zero event interval, thresholds outside their finite ledger/physical ranges, and a ledger peak below committed bytes. The first tightened focused run then failed because cadence was measured finish-to-start and coalesced callers after one full-budget sample; production now measures start-to-start, so sampling work itself consumes the interval without allowing an unbounded zero interval.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw-review/warning-floor-mutant/LOGBOOK.md-15-- VERIFICATION: Twelve deterministic Swift Testing cases cover real platform sampling, threshold equality/one-over, jumps, hysteresis, stale/unavailable evidence, warning bursts, action acknowledgement, configuration replacement, 64 concurrent observations, checked overflow, history, cardinality, and recovery. The final 256-sample macOS probe measured 0.000319625 seconds total and 0.000012042 seconds maximum. Generic iOS Simulator `ReluxTunnelCore` build succeeded; recursive Swift format passed; `make validate-core` passed 518 tests in 43 suites plus the post-test build, with the existing 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues.
.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw-review/warning-floor-mutant/LOGBOOK.md-16-- BOARD ANOMALY: Both board validations exited 0 but reported `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` for this Story and unrelated `STORY-260715-1y04r0`. The developer handoff correctly moved this task to `to-review` but the parent remained `to-dev` instead of its computed `to-review`; the specialist did not overwrite parent lifecycle state.
